#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561094} :activity/id #uuid "3fc34682-2788-5d35-a598-6c561e7bf54f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049306 :topic/id #uuid "eb34afb7-9644-525e-b42b-cf82816ee5e0" :topic/math-academy-id 3195} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561070 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28c4a6e3-5da0-58a8-98e1-f77482614d3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560451} {:answer/id #uuid "725d1c02-12f5-5f02-85e7-82273cab47b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560608} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd85793-6947-508a-a2bc-51a8f84903cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560771} {:answer/id #uuid "def61838-0d97-5c99-a6a2-029dbf9530cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560802}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560608} :answer-field/id #uuid "a93c54f2-4edf-5990-a1a6-6112ce35e742" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560937} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6d2f72f-505b-52a6-90d0-77735f112651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560815} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c187c8-63e1-5c83-9092-edcee77f622b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560848}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560848} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b06de8-f439-591e-a69d-d8f31e9bf9a8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "31cb2aad-4101-56c2-adfa-13a34142aa32" :question/math-academy-id "q-340530" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{22}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-11\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-0)-\\frac{1}{22}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)$ \n$\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."} :step/id #uuid "43c884c8-fa1e-5751-bf45-58abee1b87ae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561084}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561077 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315084 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a485b2b2-9921-5fd5-bd9d-f8899940f0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313268} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2136e8-d9d6-5af6-a549-5e509b077f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313579}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313268} :answer-field/id #uuid "45a717f2-4ea4-5657-bb93-c452e09b74ae" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14b12c1a-93ae-5bc6-9fe8-42c8eda21ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312119} {:answer/id #uuid "1b4f5c80-0a03-57e7-8507-5198d48c6bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312177} {:answer/id #uuid "4693d13b-e7f3-533f-a819-ee280e597461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312552} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7359a2-3aa5-59d3-a824-65f7cf6dc11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313001}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312119} :answer-field/id #uuid "98de6f2f-ef74-5be0-a949-95ef2c54203f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "22b987d7-9005-5317-ab10-48027150c40e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341340" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(1-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."} :step/id #uuid "71d08261-f990-5825-b224-1a3b072f84e8"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561084 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "323dbbe1-3082-574e-a141-37fe7a4c73f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x-4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560474} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc6d044-465e-59bd-9043-3e7128925241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(3x-4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560564} {:answer/id #uuid "85455903-4384-59bb-81d1-d48fab31a874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(3x-4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560644} {:answer/id #uuid "b0567346-ea67-5cbd-8a39-1edf72d23033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(3x-4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560718} {:answer/id #uuid "b491bbd6-91a8-541b-af25-681e01942fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(3x-4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560728} {:answer/id #uuid "d60aa3ac-c858-5bd4-846e-6e412ce0854c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x-4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560788}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560788} :answer-field/id #uuid "348d6e77-d6f5-5569-b7f3-7f014d07ae33" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d4b053e-12c3-5e45-ae4f-2a0387470acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560465} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0c3a79-3121-56ca-bf4b-72af6e8e9456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560532} {:answer/id #uuid "50727257-50da-5481-b2ee-3b34f40e4f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560540} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec92375-06a3-5bc9-b262-125ff5792a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560660} {:answer/id #uuid "db68e230-d768-52c1-9c2e-fd83dd64a3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560794}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560465} :answer-field/id #uuid "52ed6280-fb1c-5efd-92cf-f0fa0ff719a2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20144083-961b-5054-ad1d-a5de281d1d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560435} {:answer/id #uuid "6f45090e-5cbf-5b0f-abce-8d3156c3f296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560600} {:answer/id #uuid "80d1c28b-e18c-5913-acde-187852b1e23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560638} {:answer/id #uuid "ac98a90c-ced6-5f67-a7f0-29cf297dabc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560711} {:answer/id #uuid "beb7e7f4-faf0-5ad6-870f-155a809a5272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560742}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560711} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0193b9-6155-5584-9bd2-1442c921f71c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cf16f70d-fe20-5e04-9e8c-d37751162e97" :question/math-academy-id "q-340637" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=3x-4$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{7}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{7} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{7}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{28}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(14x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{28}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(28\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ & ={a}_{7}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{7} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{7} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x-4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9aa4ea8f-14c6-5c72-8dd1-c9ce0d451eed" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561090}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561090 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a5b03d8-7fa4-5401-9f31-c0c170006fd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560454} {:answer/id #uuid "480c4aef-5346-56fa-b6d8-38a9e3d58c5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560522} {:answer/id #uuid "65fc6d60-ff84-513b-be77-831a85519a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560577} {:answer/id #uuid "9b81d004-13c7-55f1-aef5-1fbc7d19388a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560681} {:answer/id #uuid "d99e13f9-a196-576c-9387-f6d7991d38e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560792}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560792} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f775890-b185-5534-961a-edb8b2135025" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e89138a9-d6b8-5061-b7fa-8f7c0010f6f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-341218" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ for $x\\in R.$ Suppose $f(x)$ is the $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ from $x\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ to $x\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\nII. $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\nIII. $f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f$ is the $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$-periodic extension of $F,$ we have  \n\n- $f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in [0\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$\n\nWith that in mind, we examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. This is exactly the definition of $\\pi /3$-periodicity:\n\n$$\nf(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=f(x)\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, take $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=f(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=f(0)=F(0)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x)\\ne F(x)$ for $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, take $x=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})=f(0+\\frac{\\pi }{6})=f(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=F(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=f(0)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\ne f(x)$ for $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} :step/id #uuid "b9b5ba93-4bff-5cc8-b592-e21aafc5699c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561077}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561094 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2236311d-1dcf-5814-8621-6ca58ac136e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397400} {:answer/id #uuid "80766049-c81a-5e17-9add-d24c5e9a61f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397401} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2a205e-e06c-5302-98bb-33dd8ef28f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397402} {:answer/id #uuid "74af64a7-831f-50b9-989b-da92fb9efa80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397403} {:answer/id #uuid "47abc435-93f1-5e56-be4e-2906875645c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397404} {:answer/id #uuid "84fdd6c1-2fa1-53ec-9f4e-f2c79cf04198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397405}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397400} :answer-field/id #uuid "41c0a54b-4090-5079-ad72-a367200f1bb8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397399} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "576de101-4a4e-5d10-93f1-4794297dd084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397407} {:answer/id #uuid "8be2ea60-7536-54c6-8c40-2b3ca7f53e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397408} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd3c9f2-b034-51ed-b959-1917ee861c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397409} {:answer/id #uuid "a0938cb1-fa06-51a3-9682-a27947461754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397410} {:answer/id #uuid "16682102-e4e9-5e8e-b234-f5f85ae7a7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397411}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397409} :answer-field/id #uuid "acd80bdd-4dbe-5452-b9e2-03bec982eb3d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397406} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6896852-8238-5500-8785-a40ba1143f26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397413} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0541cc-7371-58fe-8dca-eb545f614b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397414} {:answer/id #uuid "610883b1-a3e9-5606-b9ae-cf0dd1218917" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397415} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3717c9-e1f6-51ef-9d7f-0c5c74af7ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397416} {:answer/id #uuid "23137492-fa85-5ebf-bdf6-f3faffc43cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397417}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397417} :answer-field/id #uuid "d466e0c2-5e9a-5545-9677-019c4fb5c4a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aa20d8e3-c4d9-5112-bd9c-ec30f6aaa6fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-340418" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{5}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{20}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={a}_{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{5} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{5} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cce0c6d6-2f7a-5100-bbb3-4f7a6f21298b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561070}}] :activity/title "Introduction to Fourier Series" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560354}]}
